      "teacher": "The data has to physically travel through something. Either you give it a pipe to run through, or you throw it into the open air and hope it lands. Those two choices have names — guided and unguided — and knowing which to use where is most of this topic.",
      "explain": "<strong>Transmission media</strong> are the physical paths that carry the signal. <strong>Guided (wired) media</strong> confine the signal inside a solid conductor or fibre — twisted pair, coaxial cable and optical fibre. <strong>Unguided (wireless) media</strong> send the signal through free space — radio waves, microwaves, infrared and satellite links.",
