        "Twisted pair types: <strong>UTP</strong> (unshielded, used in LANs with RJ-45 connectors) and <strong>STP</strong> (shielded, better noise immunity).",
        "<strong>Coaxial cable</strong>: a central conductor inside an insulator and a metal shield; higher bandwidth than twisted pair. Used in cable TV.",
        "<strong>Optical fibre</strong>: carries <em>light</em> through a glass core using <strong>total internal reflection</strong>; core, cladding, jacket.",
