      "examAnswer": "A transmission medium is the physical path through which a signal travels from sender to receiver, and it may be guided or unguided. Guided media confine the signal within a solid medium and include twisted-pair cable, coaxial cable and optical fibre. Twisted-pair cable consists of insulated copper conductors twisted together to cancel electromagnetic interference and is the least expensive; coaxial cable provides greater bandwidth and better shielding; optical fibre transmits data as pulses of light through a glass core by total internal reflection and offers the highest bandwidth, lowest attenuation and complete immunity to electromagnetic interference. Unguided or wireless media transmit signals through free space and include radio waves, which are omnidirectional and can penetrate walls, microwaves, which are unidirectional and require line-of-sight propagation, infrared, which is restricted to short distances within a room, and satellite communication, which relays microwave signals over very large geographical areas.",
